    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "therapy doesn't change the fact that the \"me\" that mattered is gone. i look in the mirror and i dont even recognize the person looking back. it's like the soul of the athlete just evaporated, and now i'm just stuck inhabiting this useless, broken vessel. how am i supposed to find \"worth\" in a body that feels like a prison and a failure?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"self\" you miss is a powerful, beautiful part of you, but it's not the whole story of who you are. Even when your body feels like a cage, your mind, your spirit, and your capacity to feel are still very much alive. Finding worth isn't about what your body *does*, but about who you *are* underneath the physical limitations. Small acts of self-compassion and rediscovering tiny joys can start to rebuild a sense of self, even in the quiet moments.",
      "source": "target",
