      "content": "The essence of who you were was tied to movement, but that energy and passion can be redirected, even if the form changes. That \"pointless\" feeling is the weight of immense grief, not necessarily a final truth about your existence. Instead of viewing yourself as a wreck, consider the incredible resilience it takes just to navigate this day, which is a profound act of being. Perhaps the next chapter of your self is one that honors that strength in a different, quieter way.",
      "source": "target",
